# PHASE 3: P2 RELIABILITY, PERFORMANCE, OBSERVABILITY

## Reliability and error handling
- **R-1 No error boundary `[CODE]`:** add an `ErrorBoundary` around the app in `main.tsx` (friendly fallback, "Reload" and "Copy error ID" buttons, no stack trace), plus `window.addEventListener('error'|'unhandledrejection')` handlers that feed the logger. Wrap `Suspense` lazy imports with retry: on a chunk-load failure (`Failed to fetch dynamically imported module`), reload once, guarded by a `sessionStorage` flag to avoid loops.
- **R-2 Offline/hanging writes `[CODE]`:** Firestore `setDoc` resolves only on server acknowledgement; offline it hangs forever and the check-in spinner never ends, and the queued write may later commit or be rejected after the window closed. For check-in: if `navigator.onLine === false` fail fast with "You're offline"; otherwise race the write against a 12 s timeout with a clear "Taking longer than expected, please check your connection" state and a retry that is safe thanks to deterministic IDs. Give the same treatment to other critical writes.
- **R-3 AuthContext races `[CODE]`:** `attachUserListeners` is called from `onAuthStateChanged`, from `signInWithGoogle`, and from `refreshProfile`, so listeners are attached 2-3 times. `loadMemberData` re-subscribes the member listener on **every** user-doc snapshot (each read-receipt update tears it down and rebuilds it), and `checkIsAdmin` re-reads on every snapshot. A user who signs out mid-initialisation can have state set afterwards. Refactor: one attach path (auth state change), keep unsubscribers in refs, re-subscribe the member only when `memberId` changes, ignore results if the auth user changed (token/UID guard), and add error callbacks. `checkIsAdmin` for non-admins reads `admins/{uid}`, which the rules deny for them; that is why it works only through its catch, so make this explicit (or resolve admin status through a rule-permitted read) and remove the console noise.
- **R-4 Popups `[CODE]`:** `signInWithPopup` is blocked by many mobile browsers and embedded webviews. On `auth/popup-blocked` / `auth/operation-not-supported-in-this-environment`, fall back to `signInWithRedirect` with a clear message.
- **R-5 Silent failures `[CODE]`:** `handleApproveMembershipRequest`, `handleRejectMembershipRequest`, `handleUpdateSessionStatus` only `console.error`; `SessionsView` calls `handleRecordCheckIn(...)` fire-and-forget (unhandled rejection, no feedback). Surface every failure with a toast/inline `role="alert"` message and a retry where it is safe. Add double-submit protection (disabled while pending) to every mutating button.
- **R-6 Fixed fallback profile `[CODE]`:** `App` builds a fake `Member` with `id: user.uid` for admins without a linked roster record and feeds it to the home view and the edit-profile modal, which then writes to a non-existent member. Replace with an explicit "Link your roster profile" call to action; hide self check-in and self profile editing until linked.

## Performance and scalability
Targets (mobile, mid-range phone, 4G, measured with Lighthouse and a manual stopwatch):
- LCP ≤ 2.5 s; INP ≤ 200 ms; CLS ≤ 0.1.
- Initial JS ≤ 250 KB gzip (currently ≈ 290 KB). Participation chart chunk loads only on that tab.
- Check-in round trip (scan → confirmation) p95 ≤ 1.5 s on a good connection.
- Firestore reads per active member session ≤ 100 per hour (the reminder sweep alone currently exceeds this by orders of magnitude).
Required work:
- **P-1:** apply the listener scoping from P0-6; for admins bound the high-volume listeners: check-ins from the earliest month of interest (default: current and previous 2 months via `where('monthKey','>=',...)`, with an explicit "Load all history" action used for all-time stats and leaderboard recompute); sessions from 12 months back plus all upcoming. Document the threshold (above ~3,000 check-in docs) at which server-side aggregation (optional Cloud Function) becomes worthwhile; do not build it now.
- **P-2:** `MemberHomeView` calls `computeMemberStats` on every render with no `useMemo` (0 memos in that file). Memoise on `[member.id, sessions, checkIns]` and use the `useNow` hook (60 s) instead of a hand-rolled interval. In `MembersView` and `MonthlyParticipationView` verify the existing `useMemo` dependency arrays are correct and not rebuilt each snapshot (pre-index check-ins by `memberId` and `sessionId` in one pass, not `filter` per member).
- **P-3:** remove the duplicate `users` listeners (the app-level `subscribeToUsers` for admins and `PendingRequests`' own subscription).
- **P-4:** `server.ts`: `fs.existsSync(indexPath)` on every request → check once at startup (re-check only when missing). Use `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable` for hashed `/assets/*`, and `no-cache` for `index.html`, `sw.js` and `manifest.webmanifest`. The current blanket `maxAge: '1d'` also caches `sw.js` and the manifest. Add gzip/brotli (`compression` is an allowed dependency here; ~50% fewer bytes over the wire with no CDN in front).
- **P-5:** lazy-load the three-font Google Fonts request (preconnect `fonts.googleapis.com` too; trim unused weights); consider self-hosting if CSP allows.
- **P-6:** reduce `QRScannerModal` cost (148 KB): confirm `jsqr` loads only when the scanner opens and that the video/canvas/animation loops stop on close (check cleanup of `requestAnimationFrame`, `getUserMedia` tracks, wake lock, touch listeners).
- Keep private attendance data out of any cache: do not add HTTP/SW caching for Firestore responses.

## Deployment, observability, monitoring
- **O-1 Server hardening `[CODE]`:** add an Express error-handling middleware (JSON for `/api`, generic HTML otherwise, never stack traces), `SIGTERM`/`SIGINT` graceful shutdown with `server.close`, a request logger that emits **JSON lines** to stdout (method, path, status, ms, no query strings or tokens), `app.set('trust proxy', 1)`, and unknown `/assets/*`/file-extension paths returning **404** instead of the SPA `index.html` with HTTP 200 (today a stale hashed JS URL returns HTML with status 200).
- **O-2 Service worker `[CODE]`:** `public/sw.js` uses a constant cache name `dob-shell-v1`, precaches `/` and `/index.html`, and cache-first-stores **any** same-origin 200 response. Combined with O-1, a post-deploy request for an old chunk can cache the SPA HTML under a `.js` URL and permanently break the app. Fix: version the cache name from the build (inject a hash at build time), delete old caches on activate, cache only static assets whose `content-type` matches the extension (never `text/html` for a script/style/image request), cap the runtime cache size/entries, make navigations network-first with the precached shell as the only offline fallback, never intercept `/api`, Firebase, or `sw.js`, and show "A new version is available — Refresh" instead of silent `skipWaiting` mid-session.
- **O-3 Client error reporting:** add `POST /api/client-error` (body ≤ 4 KB, rate limit by IP in memory, e.g. 20/min) that writes a JSON log line to stdout (Cloud Run Logging picks it up). The client logger sends sanitised errors (message, stack, route, app version, no emails/tokens/UIDs). Optional later: forward to a monitoring tool.
- **O-4 Health:** keep `/_healthz`; make `/api/health` return only `{status}` (no uptime). Add `X-App-Version` header from a build-time constant.
- **O-5 Environment:** `.env.example` has `APP_URL` and `VITE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL`. Document that **`VITE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` must be the canonical public URL for QR deep links** (otherwise QR codes generated in the AI Studio preview point at the preview origin). Warn in the kiosk if the origin looks like a preview URL.
- **O-6 CI/CD `[CODE]`:** add `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (Node LTS): install, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, rules tests on the emulator, `npm run build`, and fail on high-severity `npm audit --omit=dev` issues that are actually shipped to the browser. Add a `deploy-rules` job or documented command `firebase deploy --only firestore:rules,firestore:indexes` against the named database. State clearly how rules reach the live database today (AI Studio panel vs CLI) and make the repo the single source of truth.
- **O-7 Monitoring `[VERIFY]`:** list the exact Console actions: Cloud Monitoring uptime check on `/_healthz`, alert policy on 5xx rate and latency, Firestore usage/billing budget alert (e.g. 80% of the free-tier daily reads), Cloud Run min instances / concurrency note for the kiosk's burst at event start.

